The first Datatrans callback for a transaction takes a lock row in datatrans_payment_transaction_url.
If its processing failed, the row stayed unprocessed forever: later callbacks only waited 30 s and gave up,
so the order was left pending_payment until the outage cron. A missing status from the Datatrans API was
even stored as processed (status NA). Release the lock row when processing fails and treat a missing
status as a failure, so the next callback (webhook / redirect) processes the payment normally.
Requires webhook-verify-signature-and-fetch-status.patch to be applied first.

diff --git a/Model/Transaction/Processor.php b/Model/Transaction/Processor.php
